  "description": "<p>The HTTP spec isn't particularly clear, but blog posts like this:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://blog.iandavis.com/2010/11/a-guide-to-publishing-linked-data-without-redirects/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://blog.iandavis.com/2010/11/a-guide-to-publishing-linked-data-without-redirects/</a></p>\n\n<p>make it sound like we should be adding a Content-Location header when we generate content-negotiated responses.  The implication of this would be each RDF serialization would need to have its own URL (e.g., <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/resource.json\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/resource.json</a>).</p>",
